@file fixtures/tx.nw
@begin docs 0
@end docs 0
@begin docs 1
@text # Transclusion fixture
@nl
@text 
@nl
@text A tiny document in the *Markdown* dialect that exercises transclusion (§10). The
@nl
@text title, an intro, and the source section all live in one `@` chunk, so the node
@nl
@text boundary is the markdown heading, not the chunk. A later section pulls the source
@nl
@text in with `\transclude`, so the weave must cut the node at the heading, splice it in
@nl
@text place, scope its ids, and link back to it.
@nl
@text 
@nl
@text ## The source {#sec:source}
@nl
@text 
@nl
@text This section is the transclusion target. The title above it belongs to a
@nl
@text shallower node, so the copy must start here and leave the `h1` out. It owns a
@nl
@text small code chunk, so the transcluded copy must scope a code section's id too.
@nl
@text 
@nl
@end docs 1
@begin code 2
@defn demo.rs
@nl
@text pub fn demo() -> u32 {
@nl
@text     7
@nl
@text }
@nl
@end code 2
@begin docs 3
@text ## The reuse {#sec:reuse}
@nl
@text 
@nl
@text The source section appears again here, transcluded in place:
@nl
@text 
@nl
@text \transclude{sec:source}
@nl
@text 
@nl
@text The document continues after the copy.
@nl
@end docs 3
